{"summary":"The task brief requires updating README.md to provide marketplace-ready documentation in both English and Russian, covering plugin capabilities, a quick-start guide, and a comprehensive settings screen guide with an ASCII mock. Key acceptance criteria include: (1) adding '## What you get', '## Quick start', and '## Settings screen' sections with an ASCII mock of the settings UI in the English half; (2) detailing specific controls: Sign in again, Check, Copy to all machines, Remove, the weekly limit meter, Parallel chats, and per-machine chips; (3) explicitly distinguishing this plugin from the Muse Code plugin while noting that both share the provider ID 'muse'; (4) updating Troubleshooting in both language sections to cite the 'exceeded its deadline' error and state that version 0.3.19 resolves it; (5) adding '### Быстрый старт' and '### Экран настроек' in the Russian section using localized strings 'Войти заново' and 'недельного лимита'; and (6) ensuring validation script 'node /tmp/muse-readme/check.mjs' passes with exit code 0. Scope is strictly confined to README.md without code changes or image files.

The supplied excerpt from README.md (lines 1–498) details the technical mechanics, architecture, CLI, and configuration of the connector, but does not yet meet the new marketplace and settings guide structure. In the English half, README.md currently covers high-level operation ('## How it works'), manual installation ('## Install'), account management ('## Accounts'), parallel slots ('### Parallel slots'), ACP agent behavior ('## The agent in BB chats'), CLI commands, environment variables, measured performance benchmarks, limits/risks, troubleshooting, and development pointers. The Russian section ('## По-русски') mirrors the technical sections ('### Как это устроено', '### Установка', '### Аккаунты', '#### Параллельные слоты') and truncates mid-sentence at line 498 in '### Агент в чатах BB'.

Crucially, the current README lacks the requested user-oriented sections: '## What you get', '## Quick start', and '## Settings screen', has no ASCII mockup of the settings interface, lacks coverage of the weekly limit meter and per-machine status chips, does not mention the Muse Code plugin disambiguation, does not mention the 'exceeded its deadline' troubleshooting entry for 0.3.19, and lacks the corresponding Russian sections '### Быстрый старт' and '### Экран настроек'. Furthermore, while the task brief lists `i18n.ts`, `app.tsx`, and `server.ts` under read_first, their source code was omitted from the host-read execution packet.","keyFacts":["README.md: Muse AI connector registers Muse (muse.ai) as a BB provider, streaming responses from a Muse side chat into BB with local tools, MCP servers, and skills.","README.md: The plugin requires Node 22+, npm, and Google Chrome on at least one connected machine (macOS or Linux), operating under the Apache-2.0 license.","README.md: By default, the connector communicates via an API transport over HTTPS and a Noise_XX_25519_AESGCM_SHA256 encrypted WebSocket tunnel directly to the user's Muse VM without needing Chrome per message.","README.md: Google Chrome (via playwright-core) serves as the sign-in mechanism and fallback transport when cookies are missing or HTTP 401/403 errors occur.","README.md: The BB host launches `muse-acp` via stdio ACP, which bridges each BB session to a Muse side chat and coordinates local tool executions.","README.md: Connector state is stored in `~/.muse-bridge/` (configurable via `MUSE_BRIDGE_HOME`), containing `accounts.json`, Chrome profiles, cookies (mode 0600), slot locks, and `sessions.json`.","README.md: Account management features include Add account, Check/Check all, Copy to all machines, Remove (with optional Chrome profile deletion), Refresh, and SSH-based sync to non-BB machines.","README.md: Accounts support parallel chats via `maxParallel` (default 1, range 1–50), using slot locks in `~/.muse-bridge/locks/` that expire after 30 minutes or process exit.","README.md: The agent communicates tool calls using fenced ```muse-tool blocks (up to 8 per reply), supporting local filesystem/bash tools, MCP servers (`mcp__<server>__<tool>`), and directory-based skills.","README.md: System instructions and project rules forwarded from BB to Muse are capped at 16 KB, and tool execution loops are limited to `MUSE_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS` (default 60).","README.md: Action approval dialogs from Muse are automatically answered with 'Always allow', whereas money/payment/subscription approvals are left for manual user intervention.","README.md: Supported models are `muse-spark` (default text/tool model) and `muse-image` (generates images saved locally to `<workspace>/muse-images/`).","README.md: The settings UI at BB Settings → Plugins → Muse lists connected machines (runtime, Chrome, agent status) and shared accounts in English or Russian.","README.md: The repository structure includes `server.ts` (hub plugin entry/RPC), `host.ts` (machine host entry), `app.tsx` and `i18n.ts` (settings UI), `bin/` (CLI and ACP agent), and `bridge/` (shared ESM modules).","README.md: The Russian documentation section begins at line 203 with `# По-русски`, currently translating technical overview, installation, accounts, and agent mechanics until truncating at line 498."],"openQuestions":["What exact visual structure, labels, and ASCII layout for the settings screen are expected by the acceptance criteria and `/tmp/muse-readme/check.mjs`, given that `app.tsx` was not provided in the excerpts?","What are the exact English and Russian localized strings defined in `i18n.ts` for controls like Sign in again ('Войти заново'), weekly limit meter ('недельного лимита'), Check, Copy to all machines, and per-machine chips?","What specific assertion checks, regex patterns, or section headers are tested in `/tmp/muse-readme/check.mjs`?","What content exists in `README.md` beyond line 498 in the untruncated file?","Should '## Quick start' and '### Быстрый старт' replace the existing '## Install' and '### Установка' sections, or are they distinct sections to be placed before/alongside them?","Where in the text should the distinction between this connector and the Muse Code plugin (sharing provider id 'muse') be stated?","Under what specific scenario does the 'exceeded its deadline' error occur, and what exact phrasing is expected for the note indicating that version 0.3.19 fixes it?"]}
